Cell["\<\
Below the threshold the most visited extension is far from a segment; at the \
threshold the excess drops to zero and stays there. The most visited member \
jumps from a walk near the germ to a segment.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"57ff9225-89bc-4829-b436-ea198081f5a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The trihexagonal tiling straightens first, at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "*"], "=", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f4cca7b-feac-4a5b-af5c-7e96cbec10d2"],
 ", then the rhombitrihexagonal tiling at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "*"], "=", "5"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a3ea21a-3b27-478d-b35b-4435a090630f"],
 ", then the truncated square tiling at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "*"], "=", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27671a66-aac6-4dfd-be66-69973c6f50ab"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"cfbce9d7-9e19-4231-aa95-5aff1abebd2a"],

Cell["\<\
On the rhombitrihexagonal tiling the deviation falls at the threshold to a \
floor of 0.8, the staircase of a segment off the lattice directions. On the \
truncated square tiling it falls to 1.2 at the threshold and settles at 2.0. \
On the trihexagonal tiling it grows after the threshold, from 1.6 to 2.5: a \
straight extension zigzags farther from its chord than the bent one.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1eb74f83-962c-4273-aaa0-ecb4ed92c546"],

Cell["Open questions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0f12edae-a4bb-475c-9a9d-d6c496582c63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "[[ The inextensible geodesic at scale ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cf993daf-743d-44d8-9852-9613ebbc6172"],
 " as an object: the infinite walks of the window graph from the germ's \
window. Is its most visited member eventually a ray at every scale above ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "*"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f59324ef-825a-4ce0-90af-1530600c208c"],
 ", and how does ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "*"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c6c64983-c337-4236-89c5-62db9fcae783"],
 " depend on the length of the germ? ]]"
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3c9b2830-c19c-4416-ad07-58f043bf436f"],

Cell["\<\
[[ The loss of direction on a lattice: the straight members follow the cone, \
not the germ. Does a mesh or a sprinkling, with no preferred directions, \
restore the germ's direction at large scales? ]]\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"78b13752-3e88-45f7-b487-bb2f8933a503"],

